// Open SSM Sessions to Multiple EC2 Instances (T1021.004 / T1021.008)
//
// Three signals in one query: non-operator principal, fan-out across distinct
// target instances, and port-forwarding (a pivot rather than a shell). The
// original query matched three SSM event names with no qualifier, firing on
// every legitimate session.
//
// REMEMBER: this shows that sessions HAPPENED, never what was done in them.
// Session content is not in CloudTrail at any verbosity. If Session Manager
// logging is not configured, treat a confirmed intrusion as full host
// compromise — there is no investigative path to what was typed.
//
// Dialect: Sentinel / Azure Log Analytics KQL. NOT CloudWatch Logs Insights.
AWSCloudTrail
| where TimeGenerated > ago(24h)
| where EventSource == "ssm.amazonaws.com"
| where EventName == "StartSession"
| where isempty(ErrorCode)
| extend Req = parse_json(RequestParameters)
| extend Target = tostring(Req.target)
| extend Doc = tostring(Req.documentName)
| summarize
    DistinctTargets = dcount(Target),
    TargetSet       = make_set(Target, 20),
    PortForwarding  = countif(Doc startswith "AWS-StartPortForwardingSession"),
    SourceIPs       = make_set(SourceIpAddress, 10),
    FirstSeen       = min(TimeGenerated),
    LastSeen        = max(TimeGenerated)
    by UserIdentityArn, bin(TimeGenerated, 15m)
| where DistinctTargets >= 3 or PortForwarding > 0
       or UserIdentityArn !has "role/ssm-operator"      // tune to your allowlist
| extend Verdict = case(
    PortForwarding > 0,     "SSM PORT-FORWARDING / PIVOT — P0",
    DistinctTargets >= 3,   "SSM INTERACTIVE ACCESS SWEEP — P0",
    "SSM SESSION BY NON-OPERATOR — review")
| order by DistinctTargets desc
//
// Companion check worth running standing: alert if Session Manager logging is
// turned OFF (the SSM-SessionManagerRunShell document's s3BucketName /
// cloudWatchLogGroupName inputs being cleared). Disabling logging immediately
// before a session is itself the signal.
